          "code": "OVERDUE_INCIDENT_AS_PRIORITY_ACTION",
          "id": "1768174649953",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768174649955_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Input = {{$context.$nodes.GET_ACTIVE_INCIDENT.$output}}\n\n\nExtract all code enforcement incidents where:\n\nThe incident review due date has passed, and\nThe incident status is still \"reported\".\n\n\nFor each overdue incident, Extract:\n\nIncident ID\nIssue Subtype Type (if available)\nLocation (if available)\nDate Reported\nReview Due Date\nDays Overdue (today - review due date)\nRecommended Action (e.g., \"Assign for immediate review\", \"Send escalation notice\", etc.)\npriority : high"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 6438.900164456758,
            "y": 5995.250635401109
          }
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": true
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Initialize communication template for Overdue"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "INITIALIZE_COMMUNICATION_TEMPLATE_FOR_OVERDUE",
          "id": "1768177788385",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768177788390_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are Code Enforcement Incident Overdue Incident Analyzer. Generate a Communication email based on the rules provided.\n\nInput:\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_ACTIVE_INCIDENT.$output}}\n\nTask:\nAnalyze the provided incident data and identify only incidents that meet all of these conditions:\n- status is Reported\n- Review Due Date is in the past\n- Overdue Days is greater than 0\n\nFor each overdue incident, generate a formal email notification to the assigned Code Technician.\n\nRules:\n- Set generatingAgent to \"CODE_ENFORCEMENT_ACTIVE_INCIDENTS_SUMMARY_AGENT\"\n- Do not set a targetAgent\n- Return only the emailContent field\n- Use only simple HTML tags: <p>, <b>, <br/>\n- Do not use markdown, tables, bullets, JSON, or internal field names\n- Do not include incidents that are not overdue\n- Do not include incidents with overdue days equal to 0 or negative\n- Do not speculate\n\nDate formatting:\n- Reported Date [Incident.SubmitDate] must be shown as YYYY-MM-DD only\n- Review Due Date [Incident.ReviewDueDate]  must be shown as YYYY-MM-DD only\n- If a date contains time or timezone data, remove everything after the date portion\n- Do not display timestamps\n\nOverdue day calculation:\n- Overdue Days = whole number of days between today and Review Due Date\n- Use the system current date: {{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\n- Never calculate from Reported Date\n- If Review Due Date is today or in the future, exclude the incident entirely\n\nOutput Structure (STRICT):\nemailContent:\nRich-text email body using only HTML markers (<p>, <b>, <br/>)\n\nFormat the email like this:\n\n<p><b>Incident Review Summary</b></p>\n<p><b>Dear Code Technician,</b></p>\n<p>The following incidents are in Reported status with overdue review dates:</p>\n\n<p><b>Incident ID:</b> [Incident ID]<br/>\n<b>Reported Date:</b> [SubmitDate in YYYY-MM-DD format]<br/>\n<b>Review Due Date:</b> [ReviewDueDate in YYYY-MM-DD format]<br/>\n<b>Overdue Days:</b> [whole number]<br/>\n<b>Assigned Technician:</b> [ReviewerName]</p>\n\nRepeat the incident paragraph for each overdue incident.\n\nClose with:\n<p>Please review these incidents promptly.<br/><br/>\nRegards,<br/>\nCode Enforcement System</p>\n\nReturn only the emailContent field."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 7241.760169120863,
            "y": 6094.663507799972
          }
