          "code": "SET_EMAIL_BODY",
          "id": "1768194248427",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768194248429_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.GET_ACTIVE_INCIDENT.$output}}\n\nyou are code enforcement Incident OverDue Incident analyzer. analyze the provided input data for incident review Due Date. If you find any incident in reported status and Incident review due date is past dated then your job is to alert the Code technician for same Incident by generating email.\n\ndisplay Incident id , reported date , review due date, overdue days and Assigned Technician for each Overdue incident in a row.\nRequirements\n-set generatingAgent to \"CODE_ENFORCEMENT_ACTIVE_INCIDENTS_SUMMARY_AGENT\"\n-set targetAgent to \"CODE_ENFORCEMENT_ACTIVE_INCIDENTS_SUMMARY_AGENT\"\n\n##Output Structure (STRICT):\n \n - emailContent:\n  Rich-text email body using HTML markers (<b>, <br/>, <p>) \n\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_ACTIVE_INCIDENT.$output}}\n\nyou are code enforcement Incident OverDue Incident analyzer. analyze the provided input data for incident review Due Date. If you find any incident in reported status and Incident review due date is past dated then your job is to alert the Code technician for same Incident by generating email.\n\ndisplay Incident id , reported date , review due date, overdue days and Assigned Technician for each Overdue incident in a row.\n  \n##Email Content Style:\n - Use simple HTML (<p>, <b>, <br/>)\n - No raw JSON\n - No internal field names\n - No cross-order references\n - No speculative statements"
            },
            {
              "id": "1768194248427_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            }
          ],
