          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1781749426651_userId",
              "name": "userId",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_USER_DETAIL.$output.result}}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "1781775717823",
          "code": "RETRIEVE_OVERDUE_INCIDENTS",
          "type": "CODE",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Retrieve Overdue Incidents",
            "sourceCode": "\n const incidents = $context.$nodes.GET_ACTIVE_INCIDENT.$output.items || [];\n  const currentDate = new Date();\n  return incidents\n    .map((incident) => {\n      const reviewDueDate = incident.ReviewDueDate\n        ? new Date(incident.ReviewDueDate)\n        : null;\n\n      const overdueDays = reviewDueDate\n        ? Math.floor((currentDate - reviewDueDate) / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24))\n        : 0;\n\n      return {\n        ...incident,\n        OverdueDays: overdueDays\n      };\n    })\n    .filter((incident) => {\n      return (\n        incident.StatusName === \"Reported\" &&\n        incident.ReviewDueDate &&\n        new Date(incident.ReviewDueDate) < currentDate &&\n        incident.OverdueDays > 0\n      );\n    });",
            "returnType": "array"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 6902.865017890492,
            "y": 5916.633371013602
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1781775930656"
          },
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}"
        },
        {
          "id": "1781775930656",
          "code": "INIT_COMMUNICATIONTEMPLATE",
          "type": "LLM",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Init CommunicationTemplate"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 6808.9855709651565,
            "y": 6156.368457501094
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1781775930656_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are the Code Enforcement Active Incident communications advisor.\n\nContext:\nFiltered overdue incidents are available at:\n{{$context.$nodes.RETRIEVE_OVERDUE_INCIDENTS.$output.result}}\n\nTask:\nGenerate exactly one runtime email communication suggestion for all overdue code enforcement incidents in the filtered input.\n\nRules:\n- Return zero oraComms blocks if the filtered overdue incident input is empty.\n- If the filtered input contains one or more incidents, return exactly one oraComms block.\n- The single email content must include every incident object from the filtered overdue incident input.\n- Do not include only the first incident.\n- Do not choose a representative incident.\n- Do not summarize, aggregate, truncate, sample, or omit incidents.\n- Count the filtered incidents first, then make sure the email body contains the same number of incident detail paragraphs.\n- Preserve the input order of incidents in the email body.\n- Only include incidents already present in the filtered overdue incident input.\n- Do not include incidents that are not in Reported status.\n- Do not include incidents with overdue days equal to 0 or negative.\n- Do not invent recipients or email addresses. If the technician email address is not available in the input, set the email parameter defaultValue to an empty string.\n- Use type \"email\".\n- Set priority to true.\n- Do not use markdown fences, CDATA, explanatory prose, or raw JSON outside the oraComms element.\n\nReturn the communication suggestion as a raw XML element with a single JSON object:\n<oraComms>{\"title\":\"...\",\"shortDescription\":\"...\",\"actionText\":\"...\",\"type\":\"email\",\"priority\":true,\"content\":\"...\",\"params\":[...]}</oraComms>\n\nRequired payload fields:\n- title: concise email suggestion title, such as \"Overdue incident review notice\".\n- shortDescription: one sentence that includes the total number of overdue incidents included in the email.\n- actionText: \"Send overdue review notice\".\n- type: \"email\".\n- priority: true.\n- content: rich-text email body using only <p>, <b>, and <br/> tags.\n- params: include email, cc, and subject as the first three entries.\n\nEmail params shape:\n{\"id\":\"email\",\"title\":\"To\",\"description\":\"Recipient email address\",\"defaultValue\":\"\",\"editable\":true}\n{\"id\":\"cc\",\"title\":\"Cc\",\"description\":\"Cc email address\",\"defaultValue\":\"\",\"editable\":true}\n{\"id\":\"subject\",\"title\":\"Subject\",\"description\":\"Email subject\",\"defaultValue\":\"Overdue code enforcement incident review required\",\"editable\":true}\n\nEmail body format:\n<p><b>Incident Review Summary</b></p>\n<p><b>Dear Code Technician,</b></p>\n<p>The following [count] incidents are in Reported status with overdue review dates:</p>\n\nFor every overdue incident in the filtered input, repeat this paragraph once:\n<p><b>Incident ID:</b> [Incident ID]<br/>\n<b>Reported Date:</b> [SubmitDate in YYYY-MM-DD format]<br/>\n<b>Review Due Date:</b> [ReviewDueDate in YYYY-MM-DD format]<br/>\n<b>Overdue Days:</b> [whole number]<br/>\n<b>Assigned Technician:</b> [ReviewerName]</p>\n\nClose with:\n<p>Please review these incidents promptly.<br/><br/>Regards,<br/>Code Enforcement System</p>\n\nDate rules:\n- Reported Date must be shown as YYYY-MM-DD only.\n- Review Due Date must be shown as YYYY-MM-DD only.\n- If a date contains time or timezone data, remove everything after the date portion."
            }
          ]
        },
